3 CTRY United States
1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	May 17, 1843 South Carolina, USA Death: 	Jan. 26, 1908 Columbia Richland County South Carolina, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo and History of Koger Plantation that Lewis E Parler owned: http://south-carolina-plantations.com/dorchester/koger.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis E. Parler was the son of Capt. Arnold Edward Parler and Sarah Catherine Thompson. He married about 1860 to Charlotte Rebecker "Lottie" Godfrey and they had seven children. CSA Pvt/Sgt Co.E, Inf. Reg. Hampton Legion, SC. At a
2 CONC ge 18, on 19 June 1861 Ciba, SC (Muster-in-Roll) he enlisted at Richmond, VA. 5 July 1861 and was appointed Sgt. Aug.1862. His Obit referred to him as "Capt."  Lewis served for several years in the State Legislature and as Co.Supt
2 CONC . of Education; he was later elected to the Constitutional Convention from Colleton Co. in 1895; when Dorchester Co. was formed he was elected the first Treasurer, and held the position for four years. He was involved in the suit 
2 CONC that determined the legality of the formation of the county. In 1876 he formed and commanded a "Saber Club" that was very active in the election that year. He had a Dry Goods, Groceries, Hats, Shoes and Hardware Store at George's 
2 CONC Station, SC after the Civil War.  Obit. "Capt." L.E. PARLER died in Columbia, S.C. and buried in St.George, under the Masonic Order, assisted by the Knights of Pythias, a loyal member of these organizations. They also had a daught
2 CONC er Tetyll born about 1861, no info. and another son, my grandfather, Claude Parler born Apr 1878 in St.George and died there of TB. He was married 30 Jun 1900 in DeSoto Co., FL to Leila Williams d/o James Madison "Matt" Williams a
2 CONC nd Olive Lavonia Williams.
2 CONT
2 CONT Compiled by Carrie PARLER-GIBSON (#46978018) Great Granddaughter of Lewis Parler and Granddaughter of Claude Parler. 
2 CONT
