1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT In the Bush River Baptist church records for February 9, 1805, it is stated that Jeremiah Goggins and his wife Elizabeth Goggins, John Mangrom and his wife Elizabeth Mangrom, and Charles Scott and his wife Elizabeth Scott were dis
2 CONC missed by letter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah Goggans (and his wife Elizabeth Peterson) went to Ohio in 1805 where Jeremiah died in 1807. Elizabeth and her son Daniel b 1803 returned to Newberry. Elizabeth married Joe Stewart (1792-1820) and they are buried at Shady 
2 CONC Grove Methodist Cemetery in Silverstreet. Daniel married Emily Davidson in 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth had a sister Cassandra Peterson who married James Goggans (their son William Moseley Goggans m Jary Jane Martin in 1846). Elizabeth and Cassandra were daughters of Thomas Peterson who married Abigail Richardson in 1776 i
2 CONC n Edgefield District, SC.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT Petersons.FTW  Source Medium: Other Date of Import: Jul 31, 1999
