1 NAME Peter /Murer/ Sr.
2 GIVN Peter
2 SURN Murer
2 NSFX Sr.
2 _MARNM Moorer
1 NAME //
2 GIVN
2 SURN Mûrer
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC buried on the Plantation of Peter Moorer, Orangeburg County, South Carolina
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1684
2 PLAC Buchsh Parish, Canton, Zurich, Bern, Switzerland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 DEC 1758
2 ADDR
3 CITY Orangeburg
3 STAE SC
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Orangeburgh German-Swiss Geneaological Society has carefully untied the common errors regarding Peter Murer/Moorer senior (d. 1758) and Peter Moorer Jr (d. 1790). Peter Jr is the father of John Henry Moorer. ht
2 CONC tps://www.ogsgs.org/ffam/ffam.php?f=moorer2
2 CONT
2 CONT Moorer (Mûrer, Maurer)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Peter Moorer Family
2 CONT
2 CONT FIRST GENERATION
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. PETER MÛRER (Sr.), was born in early 1684 in Canton  Bern, Switzerland and died 21 Dec 1758 aged almost 75 in Orangeburgh Township, South Carolina. Peter was from the "Simmental" (Simme Valley).1 [Resaerch Notes: a, b] Peter an
2 CONC d his family took passage on the ship Samuel, leaving Rotterdam about 11 May 1735. After a stop in Cowes, they arrived in Charleston on 13 Jul 1735. They left Charleston on 24 Jul 1735 for Orangeburg.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Tanner, a fellow Orangeburgh immigrant, in his letter of 18 Sep 1735, notes that two of Peter Maurer’s children died on the voyage: ... of those from Sibenthal [Simmental] four children died, two of Peter Maurer's and two of 
2 CONC Peter Aegger's.3
2 CONT
2 CONT The Giessendanner Record notes that Peter Mûrer, Senior was a native of Canton Bern and almost 75 years old at his death:
2 CONT
2 CONT 89} 1758 Thursday Decembr 21st died after 15 Days Illness and on Friday Decr 22d. was enterred in the Plantation of Peter Murer in Orangeburgh Township, the Body of the said Peter Murer, Senior, a Native of Switzerland Canton Bern
2 CONC ; Aged almost 75 years[3]. Note – the words “Canton Bern” are omitted in Salley’s transcription.4
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Mooree platted 150 acres of land and town lot #160 on 21 Oct 1735.5
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peter Mûrer were:
2 CONT
2 CONT +2.i.PETER MÛRER was born in Switzerland and died in 1790 in Orangeburgh District, South Carolina.6
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.ii.Unknown Child was born in Switzerland and died aboard ship.7
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.iii.Unknown Child was born in Switzerland and died aboard ship.8
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.iv.HANS (JOHN) MÛRER was born in Switzerland and died bef. 1754 in Orangeburgh District, South Carolina. [Research Note: c]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Moore platted 50 acres of land on 5 Oct 1737.9
2 CONT
2 CONT The 29 Jan 1754 petition of Peter Moorer for his brother’s 50 acre grant says in part:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Petition of Peter Moorer humbly shewing That the Petitioner’s Brother had by virtue of a warrant the 7th of May 1737 surveyed for him a Tract of 50 acres of Land ... . The Petitioner’s Brother John Moorer being long since dead
2 CONC  and having always lived on the said Land, the Petitioner prays that he may have a grant for the same;10
2 CONT
2 CONT I certify that John Moorer by a warrant dated May the 7th 1737 had a Tract of 50 acres surveyed in Orangeburg by George Haig, Deputy Surveyor, on the 5th of October 1737, ...[5]
2 CONT ----
