1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes: Inscription: To the memory  of Col. David Shuler  who was born August 21st 1794 and died April 27th 1872 Here lies the remains of an orphan boy who by his own unaided efforts attained to usefulness and respe
2 CONC ctability among his contemporaries. He was a 1st Lieut. in the War of 1812. Served as Sheriff of this  County four years. was a member of the So. Ca. Senate and enjoyed other offices of profit and honor. In all his ways he acknowl
2 CONC edged God and He directed his path. He was a true P. Master Mason a firm Christian who was faithful to his God and Country and how sleeps in Jesus. Source: http://www.findagrave.com
