1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Joseph "Joe" Stewart listed in THE SOUTH CAROLINA MAGAZINE OF ANCESTRAL RESEARCH, SCMAR, Volume VII, Number 1, Winter, 1979, CEMETERIES, No. 1, pg. 14: Sacred to the Memory of Joseph Stewart who departed this life the 28th Sept 18
2 CONC 20 aged 28 years. Signed - J. White
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried at Shady Grove Methodist Church Cemetery, Silverstreet, Newberry Co., SC. Finally found this cemetery on September 25, 2003, just 3 days before the 183rd anniversary date of Joe's death. It is a beautiful cemetery with ivy 
2 CONC covering the area. It is surrounded by dense trees, which thankfully, protects it. The land is used for hunting by some of the locals. The sign that is still in good shape states: Shady Grove Church (Methodist), founded 1800, Comb
2 CONC ined with Kadesh & Moon's Meeting House to form Trinity in 1835. Only that sign and the ivy covered graves are left. It is in good shape, but the cemetery on Belfast Road next to Mr. Longshore's property is in deplorable conditiio
2 CONC n. That cemetery is Kadesh Methodist Church Cemetery.
