2 CONT 9th Generation descendent Vera Mae Baker Holder joined the DAR in 1992 through her Revolutionary Ancestor THOMAS PETERSON. Her application states that THOMAS PETERSON resided at Camden District, South Carolina during the American 
2 CONC Revolution and that while acting in the capacity of patriotic service supplied 200 pounds of flour to Militia in 1779.
2 CONT
2 CONT Feb 22, 1779 received by Lieut Henry Caffey for Lieut Col. Early Kershaw Reg't of Militia. 200 weight of flour. Original copy in Data F. C. Stub Indents of Claims Against S.C. for Rev. War. Book U - W #540 - Lib. U.
