2 CONT 1810 US Census - Newberry Co., SC Peterson, Wm  3,0,0,1,1,0,2,0.0
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Federal Census - Newberry Co., SC Peterson, William     70   M   Farmer   SC Nancy       64   F                     SC A. J.            30   M                    SC Nancy M.  15   F                     SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 Federal Census - Newberry, Newberry Co., SC Peterson, Wm.             80   M   Farmer   2,100   5,000 Nancy         74   F A. J.              41   M   Overseer Nancy M.    24   F
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth date for William Peterson comes from an undated, undocumentd copy of a family bible record in the possession of (at one time) J. F. Peterson , copies of this bible record has surfaced many times in many places.
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY William Peterson of this District departed this life at his residence 23rd October 1866 (cemetery records indicate he died on the 22nd) at the advanced age of 86 years. He suffered only a brief illness, which consisted mo
2 CONC re of the wasting inroads of advancing years than any pathological disorder. Mr. Peterson was born in Newberry District , lived in it all his life and now his mortal remains rest beneath the old oak tree he planted himself in earl
2 CONC y life. He was a member of the Baptist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT He raised and succeeded in educating a large family of children, to who m he was always devotedly attached. He was a good and useful citizen, a n indulgent husband and father and a consistent Christian man.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly after the death of Mr. Peterson, his aged partner Nancy Peterson , left the old homestead and went to spend her few remaining days with her son Hiram Peterson, in Laurens District. She enjoyed usual health until about the 
2 CONC first of January when she was attacked with a disease of pulmonic nature which terminated her life on the 11th day of that month.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Baptist church and faithful in its precepts, zealous in its causes and like her husband, fell asleep in her faith Her remains were brought back to the old family grave yard and deposited beside her husband 
2 CONC on 13 January 1869.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: South Carolina, Newberry District In the Name of God Amen! I William Peterson of the State and District afforsaid being of Sound and Disposing mind and memory-calling to mind the uncertainty of life and the certainty of deat
2 CONC h -  - that it is appointed unto all men once to die, and being desirous of disposing of the effects with which it has pleased God to bless me, do make and ordain my last Will and Testament in manner following viz:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st I will my Soul to the God who gave and my body to the grave to be decently burried. 2nd I will and desire that all my just debts be paid. 3rd It is my will and desire that all my effects real and personal be brought to public 
2 CONC Sale as soon after my death as my Executor, hereinafter named may think prudent and proper upon a credit of twelve months or for cash if my Executor deems it best. 4th I will and bequeath to my beloved son Wilford Peterson out of 
2 CONC the funds arising from the sale of my property as above recommended Two hundred and fifty dollars. 5th It is my desire that my dear and beloved grand daughter Nancy Millls Peterson be permitted to retain her bedstead, bed, bed clo
2 CONC thing and Books,which I have formerly given her, and that they shall not be exposed to Sale as might be infurred from paragraph 3rd of this my last will and testament. 6th It is my will desire that my grand daughter Nancy Mills Pe
2 CONC terson have one third of of the proceeds arising from the sale of my property, after deducting the sum bequethed in paragraph 4th of this my last will and testament to my son Wilford Peterson. 7th I will and bequeath to my son And
2 CONC rew Jackson Peterson the remaining two thirds of the proceeds arising from the Sale of my property. 8th I hereby appoint my friend James B. Chappell Executor of this my last will and testament discarding and annulling all other wi
2 CONC lls by me before made, ratifying and confirming this as my last will and Testament. July 2nd A. D. 1866
2 CONT
2 CONT (signed) William Peterson. Witnesses: D. W. Patton, J. M . Workman, J. B. Chappell.  Entered into probate 5th November 1866.  (Copy in possession of Kelvin L. Meyers)
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Minutes of the Bush River Baptist Church July 10, 1819 Met according to adjornment 1st Took up the reference from last meeting respecting Bro. Wm Peterson case. Jehu Petty informed the church that Bro. Peterson was he con
2 CONC cerned in a state of intoxication for four days and was quilty of a series of misconduct some of which was to immodest to relate in an assembly of women and brother Peterson not giving the church satisfaction we therefore exclude 
2 CONC him from our fellowship. Adjourned. William Peterson was not reinstated until 1840.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
