2 CONT Quill (Old Edgefield District Genealogical Society newsletter), May/Jun 2005, Volume XXI, Number 3, Page 54: Linda Baughn sent some family information in response to the Dr. Joseph Quincy Adams article in the Mar/Apr issue of Quil
2 CONC l. She noted that Joseph Quincy Adams (b 7 Aug 1855 Edgefield, d 26 Feb 1921) married 13 May 1880 to Mamie Davis (b 1855). Joseph is also a descendant of the Peterson family. His mother. Clarissa A. Peterson (b abt 1823, d 19 Jul 
2 CONC 1857 Edgefield) married Richard Wright Adams 19 Feb 1852. in Edgefield. Clarissa A. was the daughter of Barzilla Peterson (b 10 Sep 1794 Newberry County, d 6 Jan 1826 Edgefield) who married 2 Mar 1820 Edgefield to his first cousin
2 CONC  once removed Charlotte Richardson (b 6 Jan 1792, d 30 Nov 1863 Edgefield), daughter of David Richardson (b 7 Mar 1767. d 25 Jan 1844 Edgefield) and Frances Williams (b 4 May 1773, d 14 Aug 1821) Edgefield. Barzilla Peterson was t
2 CONC he son of Thomas Peterson (b abt 1756. d 15 Mar 1827 Edgefield) married 12 Sep 1776 Abigal Richardson (b abt 1758, d 5 Jun 1826 Edgefield). David Richardson was the son of Amos Richardson (b 1741) married to Mary Peterson. Amos Ri
2 CONC chardson and Abigal Richardson were brother and sister.
