2 CONT Rev. James F. Peterson took charge of the Red Bank Church, of Saluda, Edgefield Co., SC, in 1836 and was pastor 42 years. Red Bank enjoyed much prosperity during his long pastorship...Rev. James F. Peterson died June 10th, 1881. H
2 CONC e was born in Newberry County, October 21st, 1796, and was baptized at Good Hope, in Edgefield, by Rev. Jones W. Coleman. Not long after his baptism he began to preach, and his preaching was attended with remarkable success. Mr. P
2 CONC eterson was a striking example of what men of moderate abilities and bearing can accomplish, when they are thoroughly consecrated and devoted to the work in which they are engaged. A monument beside this church marks the last rest
2 CONC ing place of Rev. James F. Peterson.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 Census - Saluda Regiment, Edgefield, SC Peterson, J. F.             64   M   Farmer   1,000   1,000   SC Rebecca     63   F                                             SC
2 CONT
