1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Mrs Isoline Wyche Goggans, 87, of 1126 Barnwell St, widow of James F Goggans and sister of US District Judge C Cecil Wyche of Spartanburg, died suddenly Friday night at Columbia hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Prosperity, daughter of Dr Cyril Thomas Wyche and Carrie Sease Wyche. She was graduated from Winthrop College and then spent a year abroad studying at L'Alliance Francais, Paris, France. On her return she taught Fr
2 CONC ench and German in Athens, Georgia and at Cottey College, Nevada, Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1915, she married James Furman Goggans, who, until his death in 1940 was manager of the Columbia branch of Pearce Young-Angel Company.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the First Presbyterian Church, the Fortnightly Book Club, the Novel Club, and was a former member of the Ann Pamela Cunningham Chapter of the Daughters of the American Revolution. She had lived at the Barnwell 
2 CONC Street address for nearly 50 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are a son, James Furman Goggans Jr of Whiting, Indiana; a daughter, Mrs Caroline Goggans Dixon (Joseph E Dixon) of Columbia; two grandchildren, Joseph Edward Dixon Jr, and Caroline Wyche Dixon; two brothers, Judge Wyche 
2 CONC of Spartanburg and Cyril Granville Wyche of Greenville, and one sister, Mrs Maxwell H Forbes of Haverford, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT One son, Thomas Wyche Goggans, died as a young child in 1925, and another son, Robert Wyche Goggans, was killed in an automobile accident at the age of 26 in 1952.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be at 4 pm Sunday at First Presbyterian Church, with interment in Elmwood Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nephews serving as pallbearers: Alfred F Burgess, Thomas a Wofford, C Thomas Wyche, Thomas M Higgins, Thomas B Boyle, Charles W Murtiashaw, William McIver, Charles S Manning, Louis W Gilland and Charles Camp.
2 CONT
2 CONT April 17, 1965 p8 The State
