1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} WORLD WAR II
2 CONT
2 CONT US Navy Killed in Action on Guadalcanal Awarded: PH, BSM, P. Unit Cit., Am. Def. M., VM, Amer., AP
2 CONT
2 CONT Attended Clemson College Son of Mr. and Mrs. O. L. Crum Husband of Corrie Houser
2 CONT
2 CONT There's a marker for Orrin in Sunnyside Cemetery in Orangeburg, SC beside his parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT ORANGEBURG - Mrs. Orrin Crum Jr. of Florence, recently received the Purple Heart medal awarded posthumously to her husband, the late Orrin Crum Jr., who lost his life when the USS Juneau was sunk by a torpedo in the Solomons in 19
2 CONC 42.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Crum was a son of O. L. Crum of Orangeburg and the late Mrs. Ethel Ziegler Crum. His widow is the former Corrie Houser of Lynchburg, who now holds the position of Florence County nurse. J. Z. Crum of Orangeburg is a brother. A
2 CONC lso surviving are two other brothers, Marion T. Crum in Italy and Bowman Crum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The State, March 5, 1944
