1 NAME Daniel /Strobel/ Jr.
2 GIVN Daniel
2 SURN Strobel
2 NSFX Jr.
2 _MARNM Strobel
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 9 MAR 1768
2 PLAC Charleston, Charleston, South Carolina, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1830
2 PLAC New Haven, CT
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://drbenjaminchurchjr.blogspot.com/2013_11_03_archive.html
2 CONT
2 CONT  Daniel Strobel, Jr. was the son of Daniel Strobel, who was born in 1735 in Prussia and emigrated to Charleston, S.C. in 1752 where he became a merchant and owned a tannery. Prospering as a prominent member of the German-American 
2 CONC community in Charleston, he had twelve children, of which Daniel, Jr. was the oldest, born in 1758 in Charleston. Precisely when Daniel, Jr. met Edward Church or where or what the precise nature of their business relationship was,
2 CONC  is unknown. We do know that Daniel, Jr. married Edward's daughter Anna (Ann) in Charleston.
2 CONT
2 CONT  About 1800, Daniel, Jr., and Anna moved to France, in order to link up with  Edward Church and his family. Presumably, the firm of Strobel and Church prospered, at first, but the outbreak of  the Napoleonic Wars created hardships
2 CONC  for trade and the firm had financial difficulties. Since Daniel Strobel, Jr., later became partners in the firm of Strobel and Martini in Bordeaux, France, one must assume that the firm of Strobel and Church was either completely
2 CONC  taken over by Edward Church or dissolved. Strobel late became U.S. Consul at Bordeaux and died in New Haven, CT at the age of 72. Edward Church remained in the mercantile trade and, seems to have done rather well for himself.
