1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Feb. 7, 1884 Death: 	Oct. 4, 1962
2 CONT
2 CONT Leila lived first in Arcadia, FL then Tampa and had a house in Silver Springs. She played the organ in church. Around 1929 she moved to NYC with her youngest son and his family. In her latter years she was a nurse and worked in di
2 CONC fferent hospitals in NYC. When she retired she moved back to Bradenton, FL, where she died. She married Claude Parler from SC and they had two sons born in Arcadia, FL. 
2 CONT
