1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT VITAL RECORDS: Birth and death of Hiram Peterson are taken from tombstone incscription in Bramlett Church Cemetery in Laurens County S.C.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN: rom the Equity Court Cases of Newberry County S.C. we find that Hiram Peterson is made the guardian of the estate of his two daughters, Louis a Caroline and Nancy Mills, who are heirs, as great granddaughters, of William
2 CONC  Pitts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hiram Peterson, guardian of Louise C. and Nancy M. Peterson (minors) received balance due to his wife, who died prior to the settlement of the estate. Hiram Peterson married Nancy Pitts--$103.29. William Pitts, Sr. died shortly af
2 CONC ter he signed his will on 29 Mar 1834 and on 24 April 1834 the will was proved and probated.
2 CONT
