1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT John T. Peterson, was Ordinary or Probate Judge of the county for several years, after the war. His knowledge of the laws pertainmg to the duties of his office was good and his decisions were seldom, if ever, reversed. He died at 
2 CONC his home on the 19th of June, 1880. He had good literary taste and judging from some stories and sketches of his that I have read in print and in manuscript, I feel sure that, under propitious circumstances, he might have attained
2 CONC  to some distinction in the world of letters.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
