1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Charlotte was Barzilla's first cousin, once removed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte RICHARDSON married George James STROTHER. They had three sons before George died on 8 October 1817. Charlotte married second to John PETERSON, and third on 20 May 1820 to Barzilla Richardson PETERSON, John's brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT In her LW&T of 16 August 1837, Joicy (Joyce Powell SHEPPARD) CULPEPPER of the District of Edgefield bequeathed "to my daughter-in-law Mrs. Charlotte PETERSON fifty dollars to be paied (sic) to her by my executors."
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 U.S. Census, South Carolina, Edgefield County, No Twp Charlotte PETERSON 58 F (Blank) 4000 SC; Clarissa PETERSON 25 F SC; Barzila PETERSON 23 M Farmer SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT William A. STROTHER, 38, (wife, Nancy COLEMAN), George James STROTHER, 33 (wife Eloise E. BATES), and David R. STROTHER, 36,(widower of Barsheba Ann NICHOLSON) also reside in Edgefield. These three appear to be the sons of Charlot
2 CONC te and George James STROTHER.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 Census - Saluda Regiment, Edgefield Co., SC Peterson, Charlotte     68   F                     1,500   3,350   SC B. (Basil)    33   M     Farmer   2,000   4,100   SC Roach, F. W.                38   F                        
2 CONC                         SC
2 CONT
2 CONT *Charlotte is living next door to a F. W. Richardson
