2 CONT As for the "s" on the end of Goggin or Goggan, Wayne G. Goggans (majwgg@ aol.com) has a copy of a document where William and Elizabeth (Beal) purchased a parcel of land where the name "Goggans" is spelled three different ways in t
2 CONC he same document. Apparently neither William or Eilzabeth could write. For this document, as well as one other Wayne has, is signed with their "Marks".
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigrated to Virginia in 1718. THE FOLLOWING WAS EXTRACTED FROM "THE GOGGANS FAMILY" COMPILED BY DON RICHARDSON, MAY 1982. UNDER WILLIAM AND ELIZABETH GOGGANS. "The earliest known documents of the parents of the Goggans branch in
2 CONC  America records a William and Elizabeth Goggans living in Richmond Co . Virginia in 1730. Four sons are attributed to William and Elizabeth, namely: Daniel, George, William and James. Daniel and George were born in Richmond Co. V
2 CONC irginia. In 1750, William and Elizabeth acquired land in Culpepper and Cumberland Counties in the mid-1750s. In Feb. 1766, the Goggans families obtained land from King George III of England in the Newberry District of South Caroli
2 CONC na and settled there. In 1770, George Goggans donated land for the location of Bush River Baptist Church. The Bush River Church was the church home of many of the Gogganses for a number of years."
2 CONT
2 CONT "There are various accounts of the four Goggans brothers serving in the War for Independence. Daniel Goggans was killed in 1781 by British sympathizers."
2 CONT
2 CONT "James Goggans, son of William Goggans and Elizabeth (Goggans), married Mary Johnston, dau. of Thomas Johnston and Elizabeth Jane Dalrymple. James Goggans and Mary Johnston had five children, namely: Thomas, Nancy, Mary, James and
2 CONC  Samuel J."
2 CONT
2 CONT "James Goggans, Sr. born Sep.16, 1751, died Oct. 25,1826. Mary Johnston born 1752, died 1816. Both are buried in the Johnston Famil y Cemetary at Newberry, SC."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Don Paul Richardson is SON of Lottie Irene Goggans and W. T. Richards on. Irene is eighth generation descendant of William Goggans; namely: Marion Oscar Goggans, Sulee Goggans, Th. Gabriel Spike Goggans, John Goggans, Thomas Gogg
2 CONC ans, James Goggans and William Goggans.
2 CONT
2 CONT OUR FOLKS by Maron Summer Eve P. 3 WILLIAM GOGGANS of Lunenburg Parish, Richmond County, Commonwealth of Virginia was recorded in an Indenture made October 18, 1750 (300 acres) Culpeper County Deed Book A 1749-1753; also another I
2 CONC ndenture was made February 21, 1766 together with his wife, ELIZABETH, in Parish of Bromfield County of Culpeper (the same 300 acres were sold).
2 CONT
2 CONT A seeming advantage took place in which WILLIAM GOGGANS moved his family out on wheels when the dissension commenced in the Lunenburg Parish, Richmond County, Virginia. On the other hand, new frontiers were opened in Culpeper Coun
2 CONC ty in 1749 where the grass was greener for the cattle, perhaps.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Goggans was first found in the Transcripts of State Papers relating to Ireland and last found Alexandria, Virginia, opposite the District of Columbia; however, no record of family indicated. According to the T.S. P.I. Jas. &
2 CONC  WM. GOGGINS came to Virginia together in 1718. WM. married 1729 in Va., a family man with a family and Jas.' affairs in order, however, no family was ever found for him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wills of Richmond County, Virginia. 1699-1800 page 82. By Robert Headley , Jr., 1983, Page 372 Charles Spoe, Will: 29 Sept. 1740, (6) Oct. 1740. I give the service due to me from William Hays to WILLIAM GOGGANS till he arrive at t
2 CONC he age of 21, the sd. GOGGANS clearing my est. of everything due to me; all land and personal est. to son Charles, if he has no heirs, then to George the son of WILLIAM GOGGANS; desires son to serve Thomas Turner until he is 21; E
2 CONC x: fr. Thomas Turner, WILLIAM GOGGANS, and Richard Jones: Wits: Joseph Ambrose, William Boyd, Sarah Boyd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 373 Charles Spoe, Inv. 3 Nov. 1740. p 4 WILLIAM GOGGANS, b. ca. 1700 in County Cork, Ireland, came to Virginia in 1718, d. ca. 1766 in Bromfield Parish, Culpeper County, Virginia. m. ELIZABETH BEAL b. 1715, m. 1729 in Lunenbu
2 CONC rg Parish, Va., d. ca. 1766 Bromfield Parish, Culpeper County, Virginia. Chn: (4) sons as found in research.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-1. Daniel Goggans,7 b. 1730 Va., d. Nov. 1781 on Goggans Branch, Little River, S.C. m. Nancy Williams, b. ca. 1732 Va., m. 1747 Va., d. Jan. 19, 1782 on GOGGANS Branch, Little River, SC, daughter of Paul Williams, Va. and/or S.C
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT 1-2 George Goggans, b. ca. 1732 Va., da. 1815 SC m. Sarah Butler,11 b . ca. 1732 Va., m. 1757 Va., Bromfield Parish, Culpeper Co., daughter of John and loving wife (name not recorded) Butler. Further research reveals and possibly 
2 CONC resolves Elizabeth Bailey, daughter of James & Elizabeth (Alexander) Bailey.
