2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT In George Leland Summer Sr.'s "Newberry County, South Carolina Historical and Genealogical" we find that the Goggans family came to SC from VA about 25 years before the beginning of the Revolutionary War.  Mr. Summer names Daniel 
2 CONC Goggans and "one or two" brothers as sons of pioneers from VA and Revolutionary War patriots and soldiers in the SC Militia.  Daniel and his older sons who were old enough to fight were killed by Tories.  The names of the pioneers
2 CONC  were not given but research by Mrs. Inez Bishop McFarland, a Goggans descendant and wife of retired Congressman William Doddridge McFarland of Washington, DC has found one William Goggans, origin unknown, to be the father of Dani
2 CONC el and his brothers.  Other Goggans pioneers may have come to SC also for there are many listed in records since the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thus, George Goggans, son of William Goggans was born in VA about 1700.  He owned property in the Bush River Community of Newberry Co., SC.  He was probably also a Revolutionary War veteran.  Some of his sons were veterans.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "South Carolina Baptists" by Leah Thompson, George Goggans gave land for a Baptist meeting house 30 x 24 ft. built in 1770 from his survey of 30 Jun 1770 on Beaverdam Branch of Bush River.  Goggans owned 250 acres tot
2 CONC al, west of James Williams (Plat X, p. 127)
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of George Goggans South Carolina - In the name of God Amen, I George Goggans of Newberry District the State & District aforesaid being sick of body but in sound & perfect memory & knowing that it is appointed for all men once
2 CONC  to die & after death to come to judgement. I therefore recommend my body to the Earth & Soul to God who gave it & as to my temporal estate which it hath pleased God to bestow on me I give & dispose of as followeth----------------
2 CONC -------------- Viz, First of all my will is that all my just debts and funeral charges be paid out of my estate, Secondly, my will is that what of my children that has not received as much of my estate as those that have married &
2 CONC  left me that their parts shall be made up out of my estate. 3ly My will is that my son James Goggans shall have all that part of my land lying over the branch where his field is joining Daniel Butler & c. 4thly My will is that th
2 CONC e remaining part of my estate both real & personal be sold & divided among my nine children allowing Bettey Anderson & Jefiah Goggans one equal part with the rest of my children. 5thly My will is that my land be sold at three inst
2 CONC allments/ I also constitute & appoint my loving son James Goggans & my loving son Daniel Goggans to be my lawful executors to act for me after my decease in all things according to law: This being my last will & testament-- Revoki
2 CONC ng & disannuling all other former wills & c. Ratifying and confirming this alone; In witnefs whereof I have hereunto set my hand & seal this 15th day of January 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Goggans Witn efses present Wm Satterwhite David Johnson Joseph Davenport
2 CONT
2 CONT Recorded in Will Book "F" Page 1. Recorded Dec. 10, 1815 Proved Dec. 11th, 1815 Test. Jas. Farnandis. O.N. D. Box No. 28, Pkg No. 59, Est. No. 663
