1 NOTE {geni:about_me} JAMES GOGGANS, b. September 16, 1751, Virginia; d. October 25, 1826, South Carolina, married Mary Johnson, d/o Thomas Johnson Jr. & Elizabeth Jane Dairymple. Daniel and George were born in Richmond Co. VA. William 
2 CONC Jr. and James were born in Culpepper Co. VA. William Sr. died about 1766 in Culpepper Co. VA. In 1766, the four Goggans brothers obtained land from King George III of England in Newberry District of South Carolina and moved (via t
2 CONC he Great Wagon Road of the Irish) their families there. Indian treaties in early 1760s opened up land for settlement in both Kentucky & in the Carolinas.
