1 NOTE {geni:about_me} WILLIAM ALBERT LAVENDER, Pvt Co F, 6th Texas Cavalry, Ross' Brigade.  Enlisted 20 Oct 1862 at Camp Holly Springs, MS. Listed on roll of prisoners dated May 1865 Jackson, MS when Gen. Richard Taylor surrendered the 
2 CONC Dept. of AL, MS, and Eastern LA to Federal Gen. Canby at Citronelle, AL, 04May1865.  One of six brothers of whom all fought for the Confederacy. Father was Archibald McCravy Lavender, mother was Sarah L. Buffington. Came to TX wit
2 CONC h his parents in 1846 settling in the Lancaster area.  Married in Ellis county, TX 21 Dec 1865 to his cousin, Margaret E. Crum. Single family marker on grave. Survived by 3 daughters and one son.
