2 DATE 6 AUG 1661
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pankraz was, in his time, the most important Frauenfelder (and perhaps person) of Henggart. He was an Amtsfahn rich, Dorfvierer, Aufseher der Schule and Herrschafts-Fahnrich. Although Fahnrich (a with u mlaut !) is
2 CONC  a military rank to compare with a sub-lieutenant, I think that Amtsfahnrich the highest official was of Henggart. Later they called such a man 'President". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pankraz was also a Dorfvierer member - and probably the chairman - of the tribunal which managed the village. Next to it he was inspector of the village school and last but not least he became the highest official of the region. H
2 CONC e still had left some time for developing a family, for he had seven children as you know. But he had also six servants and farmhands. He was indeed an important man.
