1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/3096506/person/24667357573 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 13 2022, 15:48:22 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Dallas Morning News (of Dallas, Texas) - May 8, 1900 – Page: 4
2 CONT
2 CONT      Fairfield, Tex., May 7 – John H. Blackman [Blackmon], son of County Surveyor T. G. Blackman [Blackmon], was drowned in Holder's Lake, about seven miles from Fairfield, this afternoon.  Some friends who went out at once have j
2 CONC ust returned to town and state that his body was recovered in fifteen feet of water.
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT THE FAIRFIELD RECORDER - May 11, 1900
2 CONT A SAD ACCIDENT
2 CONT A Prominent Young Man Loses His Life By Drowning
2 CONT Our little town was thrown into a state of excitement last Monday evening by the shocking news that Mr. John H. Blackmon had been drowned in Holder Lake about seven miles south-east of Fairfield. In a few moments everything was in
2 CONC  commotion, and many friends and relatives of the unfortunate young man were soon on horseback or in vehicles hurrying to the lake as fast as possible, two 
2 CONT physicians also accompanying them.
2 CONT The particulars of the accident, briefly stated, are about as follows: The deceased, in company with Mr. Murray and Mr. Joe Roller were at the upper end of the lake adjusting a seine in the water, and the deceased had mounted his 
2 CONC horse and ridden it into the lower part of the lake, apparently to swim it across. 
2 CONT Suddenly it seems, he was thrown off, and was seen to be struggling in the water. Mr. Roller ran to his assistance, and swam to him after he had sunk twice. The drowning man caught him around the neck, and pulled him under the wat
2 CONC er, and Mr. Roller was obliged to release himself and swim out. Before the rescuing party from town reached the lake other persons, white and colored living near, got there and numerous attempts had been made by diving to 
2 CONT find the body, but as such efforts were unsuccessful (sic). Finally a rope was stretched across the water and using it for a guide the bottom of the lake was dragged with hooks, and the body recovered. Although it had been in the 
2 CONC water about three hours the doctors worked a long while trying to resuscitate it, but it was impossible to do so.
2 CONT The deceased was a well known young man in our town and county, having been born and reared in Freestone. He was about 24 years old, the eldest son of Mr. T. G. Blackmon, our County Surveyor. He was a practical surveyor himself, a
2 CONC nd assisted his father in much of his work. He was married about two years ago to Miss Kate Robinson, daughter of Mr. J. P. Robinson, of Fairfield.
2 CONT The news of the untimely death of our young townsman was a painful shock to our entire community, and deepest sympathy with his family and relatives was expressed by all. Intelligent, energetic and industrious, he had just entered
2 CONC  the morning of manhood, buoyed by the hopes and promises that come to all young men that have an aim in life. His tragic death was truly unfortunate, and has 
2 CONT cast a deep shadow over many loving hearts, utterly unprepared for the sudden and unexpected change.
2 CONT The remains of the deceased were interred last Tuesday evening in the Fairfield cemetery, Rev. J. W. Holt officiating, assisted by Rev. J. M. Martin. It was a peculiarly sad burial scene. The unexpectedness of the sad occurrence, 
2 CONC the young age of the deceased, the sudden severance of domestic ties, the blighting of fond hopes---all these cast a shadow of sorrow and sympathy over the faces of everyone present on the sad occasion. The sincere condolence of a
2 CONC ll our people goes out to the bereaved ones in their sore loss of husband, son, brother and kinsman.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18191467/john-holman-blackmon Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/pro
2 CONC jects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 13 2022, 15:53:00 UTC''
