1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Evening Star (Washington (DC), District of Columbia) Tuesday, July 28, 1936
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Wannamaker - Here 15 years, Dies - Was a Member of Women's Guild of Central Union Mission
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Cornelia C Wannamaker, 79, widow of Lawton Hayne Wannamaker, Sr, and for the past 15 years a resident of this city, died last night after a short illness at her home, 250 Farragut Street.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Wannamaker was a member of the Women's Guild of Central Union Mission and attended Zion Lutheran Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Charleston, SC, Mrs Wannamaker lived a number of years in Orangeburg, SC until some time after the death of her husband.  She had been living here with her daughter, Miss Claudine Wannamaker.
2 CONT
2 CONT She leaves another daughter, Mrs Harry Smoak, Orangeburg, 4 sons, H H and A T Wannamaker both of Orangeburg and Sgt F S Wannamaker, USA stationed at Fort Hamllton, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial in Orangeburg, SC
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
