1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Feb. 15, 1921 New York New York County (Manhattan) New York, USA Death: 	Jun. 4, 2013 Dunedin Pinellas County Florida, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert Parler, 92, of Dunedin, Fla., formerly of Port Vue, died Tuesday, June 4, 2013. Born in New York City, N.Y., he was a son of the late Helen (Smith) and Donald Parler. A World War II veteran, he served in the Army Air Force.
2 CONC  Mr. Parler was a former quality control inspector at Continental Can Co., and was a co-owner of Golden Opportunity Jewelry Store, Station Square, Pittsburgh. A longtime member of Holy Trinity Catholic Church, McKeesport, he also 
2 CONC was a member of Our Lady of Lourdes Catholic Church in Dunedin, Fla. Survivors include his daughter, Lorraine (Paul Richard) Toth; a son, Richard Parler, both of Dunedin; grandchildren, William (Michele) Stone, of Clearwater, Fla.
2 CONC , Patricia Bosnak, of McKeesport, and Michael (Heather) Parler, of Oviedo, Fla.; great-granddaughter, Amanda (Mihael) Kyriakopoulos, of Morgantown, W.Va.; and sister, Helen Wright, of Oregon. He was preceded in death by his wife, 
2 CONC Ann R. (Dudik) Parler; an infant grandson; and brother, James Parler. Services will be private and interment will take place at Calvary Cemetery in Port Vue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Pittsburgh Tribune Review 6/19/2013) 
2 CONT
