1 OCCU defense factory during WW II
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Dec. 18, 1903 Overly Bottineau County North Dakota, USA Death: 	Jun. 12, 1961 Santa Cruz Santa Cruz County California, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT From Carrie Parler-Gibson: Carrie was my mother and I was named after her, so I was called "Midgie". She was brought up on a farm in North Dakota. At age 15 the family was split up, due to her father's farming accident, and she wa
2 CONC s sent to Florida to live with her married sister. That is where she met and married my father. During the Depression the family moved to New York City with their first two children, mother and brother's family. Mom and Dad had fo
2 CONC ur children, the first three born at home. She worked most of her life and was proud of the fact that she worked in a defence factory during WW II, while her oldest son served in the US Marines. Her youngest son was also a Marine 
2 CONC in the Korean war. Everyone loved mom, she was personable and would go out of her way to help anyone she could. She often claimed to be younger than she was, thus my sister entered the wrong DOB on her tombstone. I had her correct
2 CONC  this on the death certificate. She was married first to Daniel St.Clair Parler and second to Warren Lee Bowles. She died of Cancer when I was only 32 years of age. 
2 CONT
