1 OCCU Watch Maker
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Aug. 6, 1926 Tampa Hillsborough County Florida, USA Death: 	Nov. 28, 1969 Oakland Bergen County New Jersey, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT h/o Angelline A. Paliotta Parler
2 CONT
2 CONT From Carrie Parler-Gibson (Dannie's sister): In later years Dannie was known as "C.J." because he forged his father's papers to get into the US Marine Corps. during WW II, serving from 3 Feb 1943 til 24 Mar 1943. When his parents 
2 CONC found out they got him discharged. He did the same thing to get into the US Navy, serving from 16 Nov 1943 until 18 Dec 1943. Once again they found him and got him out. Honorably discharged 18 Dec 1943, #712-01-27, as Daniel Clair
2 CONC  Parler, Jr., Apprentice Seaman, V-6 from US training Station, Sampson, NY. Seeing his determination they signed the consent and he reenlisted in the Marines, serving his first term 11 Jan 1944 til 28 Mar 1946. He fought throughou
2 CONC t the Pacific with the 1st and mostly the 2nd Mar.Div., Saipan 11 Jul 1944 to 21 Jul 1944, Tinian 25 Jul 1944 to 10 Aug 1944, wounded 3 Aug 1944, served Okinawa 1 Apr 1945 to 14 Apr 1945, during which time he received two purple h
2 CONC earts for his wounds. He was with the occupational forces in Japan and was honorably discharged Marine Barracks, Naval Training Center 28 Mar 1946 as Clair Junior Parler, at Bainbridge, MD, qualified as M-1 Rifle Sharpshooter, Sco
2 CONC ut-Sniper, Automatic Rifleman. He reenlisted in the US Marines, serving 7 Apr 1947 til 6 Apr 1950, Honorably discharged 30 Jan 1951 as Pvt. 1st class Clair Junior Parler, service #535533, Hq., 3re MCRD, New York, NY. After the war
2 CONC  he did watchmaking in his basement. He also worked at a factory as a supervisor. When one of the machines broke down Dannie went over to fix it, and not noticing he was standing in water, received an extreme electric shock of 550
2 CONC  volts at a high amperage. His heart was severely damaged. Dannie was well liked by everyone, including his siblings. He was charming, very good looking, personable, and was always there for anyone who needed help. 
2 CONT
