1 NAME Clifford Herndon /Parler/
2 GIVN Clifford Herndon
2 SURN Parler
2 _MARNM Parler
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 AUG 1931
2 PLAC Manhattan
2 ADDR
3 CITY New York
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 NOV 2006
2 ADDR
3 CITY Landers
3 STAE California
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Aug. 20, 1931 New York New York County (Manhattan) New York, USA Death: 	Nov. 13, 2006 Landers San Bernardino County California, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT From Carrie Parler-Gibson (Clifford's sister): At birth he was named Clifford Herndon Parler (Herndon being a family name suggested by great-auny Vancilla). Later in life he was baptized "John", and still later in life he was conf
2 CONC irmed "Daniel" (after his brother). Clifford talked his parents into giving their permission for him to join the US Marine Corps when he was almost 17 years old. He served from March 1948 to Nov.1952, with tours in the Korean War,
2 CONC  as well as Europe. While at Parris Island, SC, he had an auto accident. The jeep he was driving back to camp in flipped a number of times. A passing lady stopped to help, and Clifford asked her to call his home in NYC, and let th
2 CONC em know he was seriously hurt. Unable to reach the family she called the Police Department. The neighbors told the police his sister, Carrie "Midgie" worked at the local bank. Although Clifford was right near the desk when the fam
2 CONC ily called the base hospital they would not admit he was there. He was honorably discharged from the Marines shortly after. After marriage Clifford and Dorothy lived with his mother, and he worked at a local gas station. While dow
2 CONC n in one of the old fashion "grease pits," a fire broke out and he was severely burned. Later Cliff and Dot moved to New Jersey and still later moved to CA. While living alone in CA he was shot by a drive-by motorist. He later mov
2 CONC ed to the desert outside Los Angeles, where he lived alone with his pets. Clifford turned out to look enough like his father to be his twin. In the spring of 2000 he purchased a small home in Landers, CA. Clifford had heart proble
2 CONC ms and a number of operations. Clifford was killed in an automobile accident and was cremated. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Daniel St. Clair Parler (1905 - 1974)
2 CONT   Carrie Maria Swensgard Bowles (1903 - 1961)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sibling:
2 CONT   Daniel Claire J. Parler (1926 - 1969)*
2 CONT   Clifford Herndon Parler (1931 - 2006)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Cremated, Ashes given to family or friend. Specifically: Ashes given to children
2 CONT
