2 CONT VITAL RECORDS:  Birth and Death dates taken from memorial written into the church minutes of the Euclatubba Baptist Church Saltillo, MS MEMORIAL RESOLUTION FOR D. F. PETERSON FORM EUCLATUBBA BAPTIST CHURCH MINUTES D. F. Peterson w
2 CONC as born in S.C. Feb. 22, 1852 professed faith in Christ in 1871. Was baptized by David Andrews in to the fellowship of Mt. Olive Baptist Church, later moved his membership with Euclatubba Baptist Church where he remained until his
2 CONC  death Aug. 19th 1911. Where God in his wisdom has seen fit to call from our midst our brother D. F. Peterson. And where as in his departure the church has lost a faithful member & his wife a devoted husband and his children a dev
2 CONC oted father and the community a trusted citizen, be it resolved that the Euclatubba Church tender to the bereaved family its condolence and sympathy in this sad hour of loneliness and distress. Be it further resolved: That we (unr
2 CONC eadable) God' s will. And resolved further a copy of these resolutions be sent to the family and then be spread on our church minutes. Ninton Baker W. P. Hunter Com. J. A. Landers Sam W. Apple!
2 CONT
2 CONT Minutes of the West Judson Baptist Association 1888. D. F. Peterson is listed  as a Delegate from Euclatubba Baptist Church along with T. Campbell  and W. R.  Hampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Copy of certificate in possession of Kelvin L. Meyers.
