1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Goggins 1770 Newberry SC-18 Apr. 1820 Lee Co. AL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: [Believed to be] James and Mary Johnston Goggins. James and Mary are buried at Johnston Cemetery Newberry, SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Rebecca Teague died Nov 28, 1862, buried at Cherry Creek Pontotoc Co. MS., daughter of Joshua and Hanna? Teague. Joshua and Hanna are buried at Goggins Church Cemetery Bexar, AL
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Advertisement
2 CONT Thomas Bailey Goggans
2 CONT BIRTH	1770
2 CONT Culpeper County, Virginia, USA
2 CONT DEATH	18 Apr 1820 (aged 49–50)
2 CONT Laurens County, South Carolina, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	Buried or Lost at Sea, Specifically: Buried in Alabama per Anna McCord Greer Add to Map
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	134434994 · View Source
2 CONT SHARE
2 CONT SAVE TO
2 CONT SUGGEST EDITS
2 CONT MEMORIAL
2 CONT PHOTOS 0
2 CONT FLOWERS 2
2 CONT Thomas was born unto James Goggans and Mary (nee Johnston) Goggans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Johnston was the daughter of Thomas E. "Big" Johnston, Sr. 1720-1796, F/G#89604746, and Elizabeth Jane (nee Dalrymple) Johnston 11JUN1725-5MAY1785, F/G#85646460.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was the 10th child, born 1752-NC, died 1816, buried in Johnston Family Cemetery, Newberry, Newberry County, SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Bailey Goggans married Rebecca Teague ca. 1789 in South Carolina.
2 CONT Rebecca was the daughter of Joshua and Hannah Teague
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Rebecca had several children:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Goggans 10 OCT 1785 - 19 OCT 1865 Newberry, SC, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Mary Goggans born 1790 died after I24 JUL 1868 married to Levi Stephens, died after 4 AUG 1868
2 CONT
2 CONT Joshua Teague Goggans born 1794 died between 1860/70 Found in Laurens Co. 1820 Census; Alabama 1840 Census; Alabama marriage record; married Eliza Conaway 25 NOV 1839 Alabama
2 CONT
2 CONT Beulah "Buly" Goggans born 1795 died after 14 JUL 1868, married Johnson
2 CONT
2 CONT Dicey Goggans McCoy born 9 NOV 1798 died 9 JAN 1867 Cherry Creek, MS married Nathaniel McCoy born 1792 died 1859, Pontotoc, MS; issue: Nathaniel McCoy, John T McCoy, Nancy M. Falkner, William McCoy, H.S. McCoy. In the book, "Our F
2 CONC olks", by Sadie Goggans, the dates for Dicey Goggans are born 1799 died 19 OCT 1867.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Goggans born 1802 died after 17 AUG 1890 born Newberry, Newberry, SC, USA, died Cherry Creek, MS, married Mary Rebecca Pitts 18 JUL 1824, Jones Co., GA . Rebecca was born 1806. They moved to Pontotoc Co., MS from GA. Records 
2 CONC by Sadie Goggans have John born 1802 and died after 17 AUG 1868.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Goggans born 13 JUL 1810 SC died 1895 Bexar, AL
2 CONT
2 CONT While Rebecca Teague was originally married to Thomas Bailey Goggans.
2 CONT Rebecca's sister, Mary Teague Pitts, was married to Jehu W. Pitts. 
2 CONT When Jehu W. Pitts became a widower upon Mary's death, he married the widow of Thomas Bailey Goggans, Rebecca Teague Goggans, sister of his deceased wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Teague Pitts died 1836 and is buried in the Poplar Springs Baptist Church Cemetery, Ware Shoals, Laurens County, SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per contributor Anna McCord Greer, Jehu and Rebecca moved to Mississippi between 1836 and 1845, both are buried at Cherry Creek, MS.
2 CONT
