1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Callie (Ulmer) Melugin, 77 years old, was the youngest of eight children born to Jacob Hamilton and Lucinda (Vaughn) Ulmer. She was a lifelong resident of Jasper County and a member of a pioneer family of the distr
2 CONC ict died at 7:20 0' clock tonight at her home east of Carthage on route 3 where she had lived for 60 years.  Mrs. Melugin was born on December 28, 1872 on a farm a quarter mile west of the Center Point Christian Christian Church. 
2 CONC She was married to the late Samuel J. Melugin on May 25, 1890 in the county recorder's office, then on the north side of the Carthage square while the present county courthouse was being built. During this marriage two children we
2 CONC re born and this includes; Joseph Thomas Melugin and Miss Eliza Ann Catherine Melugin. Callie and Samuel were married for 27 years before he passed away due on June 14, 1917 in the home due to complications from diabetes. She also
2 CONC  lost their son in 1941 at the age of 49 due to heart disease. Mr. Melugin's father settled on a farm on Spring River at old Melugin Station 11 miles east of Carthage on the Fairview road more than `100 years ago. The body was rec
2 CONC ieved by Ulmer Funeral Home. She is buried next to her husband and her son is buried beside them.  Note* Several years later in 1983 Samuel and Callie's daughter, Eliza, would pass away and is buried next to her brother, Joseph in
2 CONC  the family plot at Harvey Cemetery in LaRussell, Missouri. 
