2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Zorn-108
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Zorn, Jr. was born between 1725 and 1729, a son of Nicholas Zorn and Anna Catherina (Lebennder) Simmons. Nicholas married SUSANNA ELISABETH UNKNOWN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children seen as:
2 CONT #David Zorn,
2 CONT # Anna Katherine (Zorn) Hutto,
2 CONT # Nicholas Zorn
2 CONT #Suzannah Zorn
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas was the elder son of Nicholas Zorn, whose estate was settled in 1750 [2] Note: Evidence is lacking to indicate that his father's name was "Henry" Nicholas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas and his brother, Henry are found on the United States Census of 1800, living in the town of Orange, in the Orangeburg District of South Carolina. [3] Nicholas is found in 1810, in Barnwell, South Carolina. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas was a private in the Loyalist Militia, signing a pay voucher on 28 Sept 1782[7]:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >''No. 138 Major William CUNNINGHAM's Troop of mounted Militia We the subscribers Officers & Privates of Major William CUNNINGHAM's Troop of mounted Militia, have received in Charles Town by order of Lt. General LESLIE, of Robert 
2 CONC GRAY P.M.M. the Sums annexed to our respective Names in the right hand Colum[n] below upon the Dates prefixed thereto, having also signed a duplicate hereof the same for 92 days pay from the 8th of April to the 8th of July inclusi
2 CONC ve as per Abstract No. 138.'' (signed) Nicholas Zorn." [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas surveyed a grant of 200 acres on 6 Apr 1773[11] and it was granted on 26 Jul 1774[12]. Nicholas was on the 1778-9 jury list as a juror living "below Orangeburgh"[5]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT #https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Zorn-108
