1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Ann-Hutto/6000000007141218970 who married https://www.geni.com/people/Corp-Henry-Hutto/6000000007141045985?through=356717883180004714
2 CONT
2 CONT Was she the same as  https://www.geni.com/people/Ann-Stivender/6000000046573431838?through=6000000041115647847 ?
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Katherine Zorn, daughter of Nicholas Zorn & Susannah Elizabeth, married Henry Hutto (d 1833).   Don’t confuse with her cousin Ann Zorn, daughter of Henry Zorn & Elizabeth, who married Henry Hutto (d 1817), son of Charles Hutt
2 CONC o & Ann Tsudi.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=129704398
2 CONT
2 CONT As with Henry, there were 2 Ann Zorns. Our Ann Zorn, who married Henry Hutto was born about 1760 in Barnwell and was the daughter of Henry and Elizabeth Zorn. '''The other Ann Zorn, Anne Katherine Zorn, (this one) was born 23 Sep 
2 CONC 1758 in Blackville, Barnwell District and was the daughter of Nicolas and Susannah Elizabeth Zorn.''' Her birth is recorded in the Book of Record by Rev Giessendanner. [This Ann Zorn married Johann Ebenhard Stivender. These 2 Ann'
2 CONC s were 1st cousins also, their fathers, Nicholas and Henry Zorn being brothers. The 2 Ann's were probably named after their paternal grandmother whose name was Anna Catharina with their paternal grandfather being Nicholas Zorn who
2 CONC  immigrated to SC from Germany around 1735, around the same time our progenitor Issac Hutto with family arrived.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peter Hutto and Margaret Barbara Shuler:
2 CONT
2 CONT iv (John) Henry Hutto Henry, son of Peter and Margaret Barbara Shuler Hutto, baptized 12/25/1752; died AFT 1833, Georgia.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1817 he moved to Laurens Co Ga., and later to Williamson Co Ga. by 1820. He was living in Baker Co Ga in 1830 and there applied for a Rev War pension in 1831.A pension was denied as he had lost his discharge papers.He stated
2 CONC  (1831) that he did not believe that he was worth five dollars in March 1818; since that time he had drawn 405 acres of land in the Georgia land lottery, but that it was 150 miles from his residence and nearly worthless.He had no 
2 CONC children living with him in 1831, just an "aged and infirm wife".He died ca 1833.He died intestate. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The following are given as his children.(2)
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Henry Hutto (d 1833) and his wife: 
2 CONT #      45.       Isaac Hutto, b. 1781, m. Sarah ..... ca 1800. They moved to Ala and had at least a daughter who was b 1805 SC.
2 CONT #         46.       Margaret Hutto, b.
2 CONT #        47.       Barbara Hutto, b.
2 CONT #         48.       Elias Hutto4, b. 1780s, m Milly Ussary on 6 Oct 1814 in Laurens Co Ga.He was living 1820 Laurens Co, got land in the 1820-21 land lottery there,moved to Bates Co Ga by 1830.No children shown either census.
2 CONT #         49.       Henry Hutto, b. 1787, marr Catharine Bullock 21 July 1816 Laurens Co Ga. Not found 1820 Laurens census.
2 CONT #       50.       Ann Hutto, b. 17.., probably marr David Scott 23 Feb 1817 Laurens Co Ga.
2 CONT #       51.       John Hutto, b. ca 1796, marr Polly Ussary 1 Sept 1816 Laurens Co Ga. They were on 1820 Laurens census with two ch, moved to Bates Co Ga by 1830. 3 sons, 3 dau then.
2 CONT #        52.       Daniel Hutto, b. 1800, marr Susan Dunbar 1820.
2 CONT #      53.       Peter Hutto, b. ca 1802, living in Williamson Co Ga 1820, marr Betsey Warren 1 Nov 1821 in Laurens Co.He moved to Baker Co Ga by 1830 (p 17 of census).In 1850 an Elizabeth Hutto was living in Baker Co with ch, pos
2 CONC sibly his widow.
2 CONT #        54       George Hutto, b. 1787 SC, hypothetical son,was living close to John Hutto (above) in the 1820 Laurens census, and is found in 1830 in Baker Co. with 3 sons.1850 Early Co Ga, age 63, p332   a) Martin Hutto, b 1826
2 CONC  GA is a probable son- see 1850 census
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
