1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nicholas Zorn lll  Born c 1765 in Orangeburg, Orangeburg, South Carolina married Susannah Elizabeth (unknown).  Died 1821 in Barnewell County, South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from Upson-Talbot County GaArchives Biographies.....Zorn, James December 28 1807 - December 18 1881 < [http://files.usgwarchives.net/ga/upson/bios/gbs27zorn.txt link] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Henry Zorn, Sr. (d 1800) and Elizabeth (unknown) were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.  NICHOLAS ZORN III b. 1780 [NO] in Orangeburg SC d.	1821 Barnwell SC
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:  SUSANNAH ELIZABETH (maiden name unknown) b. 1784 in SC d.	________________;  year of marriage, 1803.       
2 CONT
2 CONT Military:  Served 97 days in the Militia during Revolutionary War.          
2 CONT
2 CONT Estate:     Brother David was Admin. Of estate until David moved to Clayton, Ala.Then John McTyere was appointed to suceed him.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Susanna Elizabeth and Nicholas Zorn (d 1821) were:
2 CONT *1.    William Zorn b. 12-25-1800 SC d. 06-26-1876 Fayette Co. GA m. Nancy Lavinia Cooper b.09-01-1805 GA d. 05-12-1863 GA; her Parents Isaac and Nancy Cooper; m. 10-13-1819; children: Henry Allen, Elijah, Nancy Ann, Martha Elizab
2 CONC eth, Mary Ann, John Calvin, Russell Daniel, Frances Caroline, Sarah and William Jefferson;  Son John Calvin m. Susan ? with the following children: Children: George, John Otis, Matilda, Millie and Mary.
2 CONT *2.	Nathan Zorn b. 1804 in SC;m. Nancy Childs on 01-25-1838 Ga.; children: Parries Zadie (Perry Z.)b 1838,Thomas b.1843, Martha A. b. 1845; 2nd m. Sarah  Smoot 02-11-1849 with 2 children one named Sarah E. b.1857. 
2 CONT *3.	Thomas Zorn b. 1806 in SC; no information on Thomas.
2 CONT *4.	JAMES ZORN b. 12-28-1807 in SC d. 12-18-1881 Upson Co. GA; see separate page for James.
2 CONT *5.	Samuel Zorn b. 1812 in SC; no information on Samuel.
2 CONT *6.	Susannah Zorn b. ?; m. Elisha Morris.
2 CONT *7.	Sarah Zorn b. ?; m. Abram Carrel.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Zorns in America (continued)
2 CONT
2 CONT The records in the Barnwell County, SC Courthouse state that two brothers,  Nicholas and David Zorn bought 300 acres “on the Bull Pond” in the District of Barnwell “on the waters of the Little Saltkatcher River (from their father’
2 CONC s estate) being part of an original land grant to Henry Zorn containing 640 acres” And that they also purchases a 54 acre tract adjoining the 300 acres form heirs of their father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three sons of Nicholas III immigrated from Barnwell SC to Upson Co. Georgia between 1830 and 1840 As all three brothers and their families are on the 1840 Upson Co. Georgia  census. They were:  William, Nathan and JAMES. Nicholas 
2 CONC brother, David had started the migration West as he 
2 CONT left for Clayton, AlaBama before his nephews left for Georgia.  
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT #http://files.usgwarchives.net/ga/upson/bios/gbs27zorn.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT #"United States Census, 1810," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XH2S-CPR : accessed 10 March 2019), Nicholas Zorn, Barnwell, Barnwell, South Carolina, United States; citing p. 146, NARA m
2 CONC icrofilm publication M252 (Washington D.C.: National Archives and Records Administration, n.d.), roll 60; FHL microfilm 181,419.
2 CONT #https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/120530518/james-warren-zorn James Zorn (1807-1881) was the son of Nicholas Zorn III (1780-1821) and Susannah Elizabeth Zorn (1784-1800) 
