1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Stephen O'Quinn was born Jan. 8, 1814, in Barnwell District, S. C., son of  Silas O'Quinn (Vol.I). He came in his boyhood with his parents to Appling  County, and was married there in 1838, to Mary ("Pollie") Carte
2 CONC r, daughter  of Jackson Carter. She was born in Barnwell District, S. C., Sept. 27,  1814.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. O'Quinn and family lived in the 443rd militia district of Appling  County. He sold out his farm and home there and they moved about 1867 to  Baker County, Fla. About ten years later they moved again, to a farm which  he bought
2 CONC  located about four miles from Lake City, Fla., in Columbia  county. He died there Aug. 1, 1886. His wife died Apr. 1, 1887. They were  buried at Friendship Baptist Church, Appling County. The son, George W. O'Quinn, enlisted as a
2 CONC  private in Co. "A", 1st Regiment,  Ist Brigade, Georgia State Troops, Oct. 3, 1861, and was m1st. ered out  April, 1862. He then enlisted Apr. 18, 1862, in Co. "K", 54th Volunteer  Georgia Infantry, and on July 30, 1862, was tran
2 CONC sferred to Co. "C", 1st  Battalion, Georgia Sharpshooters. The company roll shows him "present, May,  June, 1863" with no later entry; however, he was killed in action Sept. 21,  1863, in the battle of Chicamauaga, Tenn. 	
2 CONT Children of STEPHEN O'QUINN and MARY CARTER are: 	i.	SENITH PERSIA5 O'QUINN, b. October 01, 1839, Appling County, Georgia;  m. (1) GIDEON LONG; m. (2) ELISHA DIXON. 	ii.	RACHEL O'QUINN, b. April 20, 1842, Appling County, Georgia; 
2 CONC m. JOSEPH  WARD. 	iii.	GEORGE W. O'QUINN, b. July 01, 1844, Appling County, Georgia; d.  September 20, 1863, Chicamauaga, Tennessee, Csa Service. 	iv.	STEPHEN R. O'QUINN, b. August 23, 1846, Appling County, Georgia; m.  (1) POLLY 
2 CONC ANN EDGE; m. (2) ROSA ROBERTS BEADENBAUGH. 	v.	MARY O'QUINN, b. April 30, 1848, Appling County, Georgia. 	vi.	ELIZABETH O'QUINN, b. September 15, 1850, Appling County, Georgia; m.  WILLIAM GREEN, August 18, 1871. 	vii.	NANCY O'QUI
2 CONC NN, b. January 17, 1853, Appling County, Georgia; m. (1)  DAVID COPELAND, August 11, 1876; m. (2) ISHAM CARTER, January 10, 1889. 	viii.	ELIZA O'QUINN, b. September 14, 1855, Appling County, Georgia; d.  1883. 	ix.	REBECCA M. O'QU
2 CONC INN, b. October 18, 1859, Appling County, Georgia; m.  EUGENE G. FLOWERS, February 29, 1888.
2 CONT
