1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martha Whetstone
2 CONT
2 CONT  Departed this life on Thursday 27th February, in the 47th year of her age, Martha Whetstone, wife of the Rev. Jacob Whetstone, of Autauga County.
2 CONT
2 CONT The subject of this obituary notice, has left a disconsolate husband, eight children, and a large circle of friends, to mourn her untimely, and to them irreparable loss. At an early age she became deeply impressed with the importa
2 CONC nce of Religion, attached herself to the Methodist Episcopal Church, of which she has been an exemplary member for the last thirty-seven years. She died as she had lived, a Christian—her friendship was strong, her benevolence exte
2 CONC nsive, and her piety sincere. To her relations and friends, we can cheerfully say:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Why should we mourn departed friends
2 CONT
2 CONT Or quake at death's alarms?
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Tis but the voice that Jesus sends
2 CONT
2 CONT To call them to his arms."                 W.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Columbia, South Carolina papers will please copy.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Wetumpka Argus, Wetumpka, Alabama, 18 March 1840, page 3, column 3.
