2 CONT "He joined the Civilian Conservation Corps in 1935 and was one of 150 young CCC men who left Pensacola at daylight. He served in Auburn Alabama and planted thousands of trees in the state. He was a cook for his unit of 216 men and
2 CONC  each morning he baked 1000 biscuits at a time."
2 CONT
2 CONT "He returned home in 19236 and later served in the U.S. Navy. From 1971 through 1978, he served four terms on the Escambia County School Board. He was a founder and charter member of the Beulah Senior Citizens center on Woodside r
2 CONC oad. He was a member of Pensacola Five Flags Chapter 38 of the National Association of the Civilian Conservation Corps Alumni and the A.L. Gray Chapter # 23 DAV. He was ordained as an elder in the Pine Level Primitive Baptist Chur
2 CONC ch in 1974."
