1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Emma Cornelia Strobel (Clark)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/272578634/emma_cornelia-strobel
2 CONT
2 CONT Clark, Emma Cornelia, Daughter of Captain Jerome Clark, was born in Cherry Valley, New York. Her mother's family name was Hughes. She entered Troy Seminary from Cooperstown, New York. in 1823, and continued till 1825. She was a sc
2 CONC hoolmate and friend of Lucretia M. Davidson – the " E.C." to whom a poem is addressed, written by Lucretia Davidson, during recitation, on a leaf of " Paley." In 1832 she married the Rev. William Daniel Strobel, pastor of St. Jame
2 CONC s Lutheran Church, New York City. She died in that city in 1833. The Rev. Mr. Strobel died in Rhinebeck, New York in 1889.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Emma Willard and her pupils, or, Fifty years of Troy Female Seminary: 1822-1872" by Mrs. R. Sage, 1898, p 52.
