2 CONT BIRTH: Noted from census records, tombstone inscription, and personal knowledge of his wife Annie Caroline Griffin Peterson. A farmer by trade, who loved to sing. Met his wife at a singing school in Mississippi and attended singin
2 CONC g conventions whenever possible.
2 CONT
2 CONT T. L. Peterson 55 died at 12:07 o'clock this afternoon at the home of a daughter Mrs. T. H. Montgomery of one and one-half miles east of Lubbock. Funeral services will be conducted at 3 o'clock Tuesday afternoon at Union Baptist c
2 CONC hurch in Union community, with Rev. J. T. Clinton officiating. Burial will be in the Slaton cemetery, under the direction of Sanders Funeral home. Mr. Peterson suffered paralysis. He is survived by his wife; five sons, Alvis, Earl
2 CONC , Luther, Eugene, and Buford; four daughters Mrs. Montgomery, Mrs. Elois McRae, Virginia and Lula Mae Peterson.
2 CONT
