3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Jackson Goodgame was born in Coosa County, Alabama, son of James Alexander Goodgame and Telitha Cobb Goodgame.  He and two brothers moved to Arkansas in 1851.  He married Martha Jane Mahan on December 25, 185
2 CONC 1.  They had three children, John Thomas Goodgame, 1853 - Aug 28, 1865; Mary Emaline Goodgame, 1857 - 1931; and Florida Bell Goodgame, 1859 - ?.  He joined the Confederate Army, serving as a corporal in the 33rd Regiment of the Ar
2 CONC kansas Infantry, Co. C.  He died in 1862 and was buried on a private farm in Louisburg, Arkansas.
