2 CONT ===Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT The Journal and Review, Aiken, SC, April 23, 1924
2 CONT Mrs. J. O. Jones
2 CONT
2 CONT After a long and painful illness, Mrs. J. O. Jones, aged 66 years died at her Ridge Spring home early Tuesday morning.  Before her marriage 41 years ago she was Miss Lucy Woodward.  She having been the mother of thirteen children,
2 CONC  nine of them are now living along with several grandchildren. Those' surviving are: A. O. Jones, of Largo, Fla., C. D Jones. of Langley, M. L. Jones of Aiken ; J. P. Jones of Ward, H. C. Jones of Ward; Mrs. J. F. Staleyof Denmark
2 CONC ; Mrs. J. O. LaGrone of Jackson; Mrs. H M T h r a i l k i l l and Miss Lucy Jones of Ridge Spring. And "two brothers : Messrs. J. O. Jones of Graniteville, and P. J. Jones of L i t t l e Rock.  Ark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted in the Baptist church by the pastor, the Rev. W. S. Dorsett. Interment was made in the Ward cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
