1 BURI
2 DATE AFT 10 NOV 1673
2 ADDR
3 CITY Providence
3 STAE Rhode Island
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chad, Elizabeth and some or all of the boys came to America in July 1638 on the ship “Martin” which arrived in Boston. The same year, Chad was one of the original signers of the pact that organized Providence, Rhod
2 CONC e Island. In 1642, he became minister of the Baptist church there; in 1644, he was the first signer of the town’s charter.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://mybigmonkey.com/genealogy/brown.pdf
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Elizabeth Sharparowe was born to Helen Margaret Sharparowe formerly Castley, and John Sharparowe  who were from Westmorland, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Sharparowe of  Melbourne, Bedfordshire, England married Chad Brown on September 11, 1626. Chad Brown, Elizabeth and their son John moved to Providence, Rhode Island shortly after arriving in Boston, where along with Roge
2 CONC r Williams and others he was a signer of the Rhode Island Compact which denied religious interference in civil affairs. In 1642 her husband was ordained as pastor of the First Baptist Church of Providence.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Sharparowe-1
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (Sharparowe) Brown (abt. 1605 - bef. 1672)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Brown formerly Sharparowe
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1605 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Chad Brown — married 11 Sep 1626 in High Wycombe, Buckinghamshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Judah Brown, John Brown, Jeremiah Brown, Daniel Brown Sr. and James Brown Sr
2 CONT
2 CONT Died before 31 Dec 1672 before about age 67 in Providence, Providence, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 26 Aug 2021 | Created 30 Dec 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (Sharparowe) Brown migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Disputed Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile previously gave John Sharparowe and Helen Margaret Castley as Elizabeth's parents. Following the sources given, the original source appears to be IGI and contains contradictory and chronological impossibilities. These
2 CONC  parents have been disconnected. No primary evidence as to her parents has been found.
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: About 1605 in England.
2 CONT Estimate based on marriage in 1626.
2 CONT Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Chad Brown on 11 September 1626 in High Wycombe, Buckinghamshire, England.[1][2]
2 CONT Children of Chad Brown and Elizabeth Sharparowe:
2 CONT Please a detailed analysis published in The American Genealogist.[3]
2 CONT John Browne. Born about 1630. Married about 1660 Mary Holmes. Died about 1706 in Providence, Rhode Island.
2 CONT Judah Browne.
2 CONT James Browne.
2 CONT Jeremiah Browne.
2 CONT Daniel Browne (possible).
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: Before 31 December 1672, presumably in Providence, Rhode Island.
2 CONT She was noted as deceased on this date in a deed of her son John.[3]
2 CONT Common Errors to Avoid
2 CONT
2 CONT Disproved son: Chad Brown: Chad and Elizabeth Brown are commonly given a son Chad Brown. This has been shown to be an error resulting from misinterpretation of land distribution in Providence.[3] After the death of Chad Brown, dis
2 CONC tributions of land continued to made in the name of Chad Brown. A son Chad Brown was created to explain these records; however, it can be shown that Providence continued to set off land in the names of the original proprietors eve
2 CONC n after their death. There is no other evidence or reason to suppose a son Chad.
2 CONT Disproved daughter: Phebe Brown: Virkus in his Compendium of American Genealogy made Phebe Brown, wife of Thomas Lee, a daughter of Chad Browne.[4] This is incorrect. She is a proven daughter of William Brown.[3]
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnotes and citations:
2 CONT ↑ NEHGR, vol. 65 no. 1 (January 1911): page 84.
2 CONT ↑ Phillimore.Buckinghamshire Parish Registers, vol. 6: Marriages. (1910): page 11.
2 CONT ↑ 3.0 3.1 3.2 3.3 American Genealogist, vol. 62 no. 4 (October 1987): pages 193-201.
2 CONT ↑ Virkus, Frederick Adams. ed. Compendium of American Genealogy; ... v.5 (1933): pages 56, 97.
2 CONT Source list:
2 CONT New England Historical and Genealogical Register, vol. 65 no. 1 (January 1911): page 84. "Notes: King, Brown", by The Editors. Marriage of Chad Brown. Books.google.com Link
2 CONT Phillimore, W.P.W. ed. Buckinghamshire Parish Registers, vol. 6: Marriages. (London: 1910): page 11. Archive.org Link
2 CONT New England Historical and Genealogical Register, vol. 80 no. 1 (January 1926): pages 73-86 and 170-185, see page 74. AmericanAncestors.org ($) Link "Chad Browne of Providence, Rhode Island and Four Generations of His Descendants"
2 CONC , by William Bradford Browne.
2 CONT The American Genealogist, vol. 62 no. 4 (October 1987): 193-201. "The Children of Chad Browne of Providence, RI: Proved, Disproved and Unproved, " by Bruce C. MacGunnigle. AmericanAncestors.org ($) Link
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial [1] updated 25 August 2021.
2 CONT Virkus, Frederick Adams. ed. Compendium of American Genealogy; ... v.5 (1933): pages 56, 97. Note:incorrectly makes Phebe Brown a daughter of Chad Browne.
