2 CONT Profile last modified 23 Jan 2016 | Created 8 Jul 2011
2 CONT This page has been accessed 743 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Judah is the son of Chad Browne and Elizabeth Sharparowe.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Judah died in 1663. Friends Records of Newport[2] reports:
2 CONT
2 CONT Judah Brown the son of Chad Brown of Providence in the Colony of Rhode Island he dyed at Newport and was buried in the place given by Thomas Clifton upon 16 d: 3 mo: 1663.
2 CONT The Friends calendar started in March, so the third month would be May. The Chad Brown Memorial indicates he died unmarried on May 10, 1663.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chad Brown Memorial[1] indicates Chad and Judah are one and the same. Friends Records of Newport[2] and [3] indicates these two different people.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
