2 CONT John Browne was known as "old goodman Brown". He lived in Ipswich, Massachusetts as early as 1656, and he was married to Mary.[5] John and Mary married before 1643 at Ipswich.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Brown(e) was first mentioned in Ipswich, Massachusetts records in 1640.[1] His wife's name was Mary. John and Mary had the following known children:[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT John, b about 1639 (about 1643 per Perley source)
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha, m Barnard Thorne between 1670 and 1679
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, m Thomas Jacobs Dec 21, 1671 (Parish Record)
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel, b about 1652 (about 1654 per deposition given in 1679 [4])
2 CONT ''''
2 CONT
2 CONT John Browne died in Ipswich Sep 13, 1677.[2][5][3] John's estate was probated in Ipswich, and in it he named his wife, eldest son, John; his son Nathaniel, and daughters Martha Thorne and Sarah Jacobs.[4]
2 CONT
