1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adrienne_Shelly
2 CONT
2 CONT Adrienne Shelly (née Levine; June 24, 1966 – November 1, 2006) was an American actress, film director, and screenwriter. She gained recognition for her roles in independent films, particularly Hal Hartley's The Unbelievable Truth 
2 CONC (1989) and Trust (1990). She later wrote, directed, and co-starred in Waitress (2007), which was released posthumously and later adapted into a Broadway musical.
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 1, 2006, Shelly was found dead in her Manhattan office. Though initially ruled a suicide, her husband, Andy Ostroy, pushed for further investigation. This led to the arrest of Diego Pillco, a 19-year-old construction w
2 CONC orker, who confessed to the murder. Pillco was sentenced to 25 years in prison without parole.
