1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Ingels, Sadie Ann Ulmer]
2 CONT
2 CONT Maryville Daily Forum
2 CONT
2 CONT Tuesday January 26, 1954 p. 9
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Services Monday For Mrs. Alva Ingels
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Alva Ingels [Sadie Ann Ulmer], Pickering, who died Saturday, were held at 2 o'clock Monday afternoon at the Methodist church in Pickering, conducted by Rev. Elmer Evans. Burial was in the Hopkins cemetery
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT A quartet, including Mrs. Alvin Trueblood, Mrs. Howard Null, Donnis Hood and Charles Pakes, sang "It Is Well With My Soul" and "In the Sweet Bye and Bye" with Mrs. Denver Loch, accompanist. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers were Mark Lyle and Lane Ulmer, Merlin McClurg and Donovan and Sam Ingels and honorary pallbearers were Ray Ulmer, Harold Dean Ingels, Eugene Schooler, Theodore Ingels, Milo McClurg, Elmer Laughlin and Haldon Dale Ingel
2 CONC s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Flowers were in charge of Mrs. Harry Glines, Mrs. Floy Watkins, Mrs. Herschel Stoner, Mrs. Dewey Evans, Mrs. Vere Hall and Mrs. Keith Men
2 CONT
