1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Everett H. Ulmer Dies; To Hold Rites at Hopkins
2 CONT
2 CONT Everett Hebron Ulmer, 73-year-old Hopkins resident, died at 4:27 o'clock Monday afternoon at a nursing home in St. Joseph following a long illness. He had lived his entire life in Hopkins community. He was a retired farmer and car
2 CONC penter. Mr. Ulmer was a member of the Hopkins Baptist church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 2 p.m. Thursday afternoon in the Baptist church of Hopkins with the Rev. Wilbur Thoriakson officiating. Burial will be in the Hopkins cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born February 17, 1874, the son of the late Mr. and Mrs. James W. Ulmer. He was married to Mrs. Nettie Ulmer, December 12, 1895. She died October 2, 1943.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by two sons, Galen and Cleo Ulmer, Hopkins; one daughter, Mrs. Verda Bridgewater, Hopkins; one brother, George B. Ulmer, Denver, Colo.; 10 grandchildren and five great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Maryville Daily Forum, Maryville, Missouri Tuesday, September 9, 1947 Page 1
2 CONT
