1 NOTE {geni:about_me} CARTHAGE EVENING PRESS APRIL 21, 1946
2 CONT
2 CONT HERBERT W. RUSH DIES
2 CONT
2 CONT QUARRYMAN, 62, WAS BORN IN CARTHAGE
2 CONT
2 CONT Services Delayed Until Arrival of Son From Phillipines-Wife and 12 Children Survive
2 CONT
2 CONT Herbert William Rush, 62, former stone cutter of the Carthage Marble Corporation, died at 1 0'clock yesterday afternoon at his home, 1125 prospect avenue. Mr. Rush had been ill since about March 1. Last Tuesday his condition becam
2 CONC e more serious and his children living at a distance were notified to come to his bedside. He was born January 13, 1884 in Carthage and had been a resident here all of his life. He was a son of the late Mr. and Mrs. George W. Rush
2 CONC . Surviving him are his wife, Minnie May Rush, 12 children; Lon William Mark C. Matt Billy Dean Paul V. and  Robert L. Rush and  Mrs. Thelma Hawley all of Chicago. Lloyd H. Rush of Carthage Mrs. Olive Graves of Park Ridge Illinois
2 CONC , Miss Faye Rush of Kansas City and Pvt. Gaylord D. Rush of the U.S. Army stationed in Manilla a brother,  George A. Rush, who is in charge of the finance department at the Carthage post office, and 13 grandchildren. Mr. Rush was 
2 CONC a member of the Church of the Nazarene. Funeral is under the direction of Ulmer Funeral Home.
