1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Well-Known Farmer Dies Samuel Joseph Melugin, 57 years old, a well known Jasper county farmer died at 5:30 0' clock yesterday afternoon at the Melugin home on the Chestnut street road, eight miles east of Carthage.
2 CONC  Death was due to complications of diabetes. Mr. Melugin was well known in his community having resided at the place of his death for the last 29 years. He is survived by his widow. Funeral services will be conducted at 2 0' clock
2 CONC  tomorrow afternoon from his home. Burial will be in Harvey Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of J.W. Melugin and Eliza Allison Melugin. He was married to Callie Ulmer and during this marriage two children were born. The children's names were; Eliza Ann Catherine and Joseph Thomas Melugin. Samuel died from c
2 CONC omplications of diabetes and from going into a diabetic coma and never regaining consciousness again. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Joseph W Melugin (1818 - 1895)
2 CONT   Eliza Ann Catherine Allison Melugin (1820 - 1893)
