1 NAME Henry /Hutto/
2 GIVN Henry
2 SURN Hutto
2 _MARNM Hutto
1 NAME Henry Hutto, of Georgia
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 DEC 1752
2 ADDR
3 STAE South Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1833
2 ADDR
3 STAE Georgia
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Corp-Henry-Hutto/6000000007141045985 who married https://www.geni.com/people/Ann-Hutto/6000000007141218970?through=6000000007141045985
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Katherine Zorn, daughter of Nicholas Zorn & Susannah Elizabeth, married Henry Hutto (d 1833).  Don’t confuse with her cousin Ann Zorn, daughter of Henry Zorn & Elizabeth, who married Henry Hutto (d 1817), son of Charles Hutto
2 CONC  & Ann Tsudi.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peter Hutto and Margaret Barbara Shuler:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT iv '''(John) Henry Hutto''' Henry, son of Peter and Margaret Barbara Shuler Hutto, baptized 12/25/1752; died AFT 1833, Georgia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/hutto/1206/
2 CONT
2 CONT This man was an almost exact contemporary of his first cousin of the same name and it is almost impossible to be sure which is which in any given record!See discussion below, as well as end note.
2 CONT
2 CONT 16.  616.       Henry Hutto3, son of Peter2 Hutto and Margaret Barbara Hutto, born 1751/2 in Orangeburg Dist, was baptized 25 Dec 1752 by Rev. Giessendanner. (5)We have already stated that records seem to indicatethat Peter Hutto 
2 CONC probably died by about 1760, before he could take out land, and when Henry was just a lad.If he went to live with his Shuler grandparents, which we do not know for sure, this would have been generally in the area around Bowman, so
2 CONC me 6-8 miles southeast of Orangeburg town.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the time this man and his contemporary first cousin of the same name reached adulthood, they settled in very different parts of Orangeburg County.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served several enlistments in the Revolution. He first joined the 1st SC Infantry Reg't in Nov. 1775, serving a second term in 3rd SC Reg't.He was promoted to Corporal in 1780.He was captured at Charleston and [possibly] held t
2 CONC here, being released at the end of the war.He returned home and began raising a family.In Dec 1786 Henry received an Indented Certificate for pay for service as a private soldier in the 3rd SC Reg’t in 1780 and 1781. When he assig
2 CONC ned this certificate over to John Murer in March 1787, this was witnessed by David Shuler, probably his uncle.His wife's name has not been learned; he would have married about 1779.In the 1790 census his family of in the north par
2 CONC t of Orangeburgh.In 1810 we find him living in Orangeburg Co, SC near Shulers, Snells, and Youns. Henry was an early trustee of the White House Methodist Church at Four Holes.( 14)
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1817 he moved to Laurens Co Ga., and later to Williamson Co Ga. by 1820. He was living in Baker Co Ga in 1830 and there applied for a Rev War pension in 1831.A pension was denied as he had lost his discharge papers.He stated
2 CONC  (1831) that he did not believe that he was worth five dollars in March 1818; since that time he had drawn 405 acres of land in the Georgia land lottery, but that it was 150 miles from his residence and nearly worthless.He had no 
2 CONC children living with him in 1831, just an "aged and infirm wife".He died ca 1833.He died intestate. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The following are given as his children.(2)
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Henry Hutto (d 1833) and his wife: 
2 CONT #      45.       Isaac Hutto, b. 1781, m. Sarah ..... ca 1800. They moved to Ala and had at least a daughter who was b 1805 SC.
2 CONT #         46.       Margaret Hutto, b.
2 CONT #        47.       Barbara Hutto, b.
2 CONT #         48.       Elias Hutto4, b. 1780s, m Milly Ussary on 6 Oct 1814 in Laurens Co Ga.He was living 1820 Laurens Co, got land in the 1820-21 land lottery there,moved to Bates Co Ga by 1830.No children shown either census.
2 CONT #         49.       Henry Hutto, b. 1787, marr Catharine Bullock 21 July 1816 Laurens Co Ga. Not found 1820 Laurens census.
2 CONT #       50.       Ann Hutto, b. 17.., probably marr David Scott 23 Feb 1817 Laurens Co Ga.
2 CONT #       51.       John Hutto, b. ca 1796, marr Polly Ussary 1 Sept 1816 Laurens Co Ga. They were on 1820 Laurens census with two ch, moved to Bates Co Ga by 1830. 3 sons, 3 dau then.
2 CONT #        52.       Daniel Hutto, b. 1800, marr Susan Dunbar 1820.
2 CONT #      53.       Peter Hutto, b. ca 1802, living in Williamson Co Ga 1820, marr Betsey Warren 1 Nov 1821 in Laurens Co.He moved to Baker Co Ga by 1830 (p 17 of census).In 1850 an Elizabeth Hutto was living in Baker Co with ch, pos
2 CONC sibly his widow.
2 CONT #        54       George Hutto, b. 1787 SC, hypothetical son,was living close to John Hutto (above) in the 1820 Laurens census, and is found in 1830 in Baker Co. with 3 sons.1850 Early Co Ga, age 63, p332   a) Martin Hutto, b 1826
2 CONC  GA is a probable son- see 1850 census
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=129704398
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT As with Henry, there were 2 Ann Zorns. Our Ann Zorn, who married Henry Hutto was born about 1760 in Barnwell and was the daughter of Henry and Elizabeth Zorn. The other Ann Zorn, Anne Katherine Zorn was born 23 Sep 1758 in Blackvi
2 CONC lle, Barnwell District and was the daughter of Nicolas and Susannah Elizabeth Zorn. Her birth is recorded in the Book of Record by Rev Giessendanner. This Ann Zorn married Johann Ebenhard Stivender. These 2 Ann's were 1st cousins 
2 CONC also, their fathers, Nicholas and Henry Zorn being brothers. The 2 Ann's were probably named after their paternal grandmother whose name was Anna Catharina with their paternal grandfather being Nicholas Zorn who immigrated to SC f
2 CONC rom Germany around 1735, around the same time our progenitor Issac Hutto with family arrived.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peter Hutto & Margaret Barbara Shuler, born at Orangeburgh, South Carolina:
2 CONT # Isaac  born 4 Dec 1750 2 sons 
2 CONT # Henry b 25 Dec 1752 d 1833 m (Anna Katherine Zorn)
2 CONT # Martin born 1 Apr 1755 no known issue 
2 CONT
