2 CONC d=153608970&pid=20
2 CONT Marriage, Maries Co, MO: Robert S Crum and Louisa V. Hutchison, both from Maries Co, Vienna, MO married 3 Sep 1905 in Maries Co, MO. 
2 CONT ****************************************** Home in 1900: Jackson, Maries, Missouri  Robert Crum 71 Sept 1828 mar 28y TN Harriet A Crum 70 wf Dec 1829 8/6 ch Eng. Robert L Copeland 18 gs Oct 1881 sgl MO Girtie B Copeland 13 gd Sep 
2 CONC 1886 MO
2 CONT
2 CONT Home in 1880: Jackson, Maries, Missouri  R. S. Crum 57 mar. TN Harriet Crum 50 wf mar. Eng. John Crum 24 son sgl MO Iora Collins 20 w/f servant sgl MO John Collins 21 m/w farmer sgl MO Wm. Collins 18 m/w farmer MO Mary Crum 20 f/w
2 CONC  servant sgl MO Jas. P. Crum 19 m/w laborer MO Geo. W. Crum 14 m/w "measles" MO Sarah L. Crum 12 f/w MO Thos. Crum 10 m/w MO Harriet Crum 10 f/w MO Jacob Crum 7/12 "Oct" MO  Geo. Stinsen 21 w/m sgl MO
2 CONT
2 CONT Home in 1870: Jackson, Maries, MO  Post Office: Lanes Prairie  Robert Crunb 41 m/w TN Harriet A Crunb 40 f/w Eng.
2 CONT *Rachael Crunb 17 f/w TN John E Coates* 19 m/w Eng *Crunb on cen. John F Crunb 15 m/w MO Sarah A Crunb 14 f/w MO Henry Collins 10 m/w MO William E Collins 8 m/w MO Mary Crunb 13 f/w MO Joseph P Crunb 9 m/w MO George W Crunb 6 m/w 
2 CONC MO Sarah L Crunb 4 f/w MO William I Crunb 1 m/w MO ---, Smallwood 21 works on farm IN
2 CONT ***************************************** Marriage, Maries Co, MO Index to Book A, #22: Robert Crum and Harriett Collins, married Dec. 10, 1868 by James Miller, JP. Note: discrepancy between date when Elizabeth [lst wife] died and
2 CONC  date recorded for marriage. [1868] See also dates recorded in King's History.
2 CONT *************************** Home in 1860: Jackson, Maries, Missouri  Post Office: Vienna  R S Crum 31 male TN Elizabeth Crum 30 female TN
2 CONT *Rachel Crum 6 female TN John Crum 5 male MO Mary Crum 3 female MO Joseph Crum 4/12 male MO Zack German 48 male farm hand NY
2 CONT ***************************** From History of Maries Co, MO by Everett M. King: Robert Sevier Crum was born in Greene County, Tennessee, September 9, 1828, and was the son of John and Jennie Crum. John Crum, born in 1778, was kill
2 CONC ed in Tennessee in a mine accident when young Robert was ten years old. They were of German descent and the family name may have originally been Krum. Robert was the second youngest of twelve children, and for many years was the o
2 CONC nly member of the family to live in this state, but he was later joined by his brother John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Sevier Crum and Elizabeth Hutchison were married in Tennessee August 12, 1852, and their oldest child, Rachel Jane, later wife of James Malone, was born before they left that state. In 1854 they settled at the farm four mil
2 CONC es north of Vienna still known as the Bob Crum place, where their six remaining children, John F., Mary E., Joseph P., Lanattie, and William J.[error-should read George W.] Crum were born. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Crum died February 1870, and in April, 1871, he was married to Mrs.[Harriett] Agnes Collins, born O'Neill, to which union one child was born, Harriett A. Crum, now wife of James M. Brown of Lanes Prairie. After the death of h
2 CONC is second wife, Mr. Crum was married to Louise V., widow of William Hutchison, nee Krewson, who survived him many years. He died in March 1906. [See also Bio in History of Cole, Moniteau, Morgan, Benton, Miller, Maries and Osage C
2 CONC ounties, Missouri, 1889].
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/61592238/robert-sevier-crum Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 20 2019, 15:40:03 UTC''
