1 NAME Hansford Rowell /Alford/
2 GIVN Hansford Rowell
2 SURN Alford
2 _MARNM Alford
2 NICK Hance
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lake Butler
3 STAE Florida
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1812
2 ADDR
3 CITY Spartanburg
3 STAE South Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1866
2 PLAC Florida,USA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Farmer, Methodist minister
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Memorial located at Swift Creek Cemetery, Lake Butler, Union County, Florida
2 CONT
2 CONT Hansford Alford was an early settler of Florida. He was a slave owner, indian fighter, farmer, and State Representative.  He came to Florida in the 1830's with his father, John Alford. Their first recorded land records are in Hami
2 CONC lton County, Florida. Later Hansford and his father removed to Columbia County, Florida which later became part of New River County, then later Baker County, Florida. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hansford Alford served as a 1st lieutenant in the Second Seminole Indian War in Johnson's Company, Florida Mounted Milita from 1839 to 1840. He also served in Day's and Wilder's Company of the 13th Regiment of the 1st Brigade of t
2 CONC he Florida Mounted Militia.  He was elected to the Florida Legislature as a Representative for Columbia County, Florida in 1856.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married twice. His first wife was Jincy Mann. After her death, he married Louvicy Crosby. Hansford Alford was said to have been killed sometime in the 1860's due to his opposition to the Civil War. His death was confirmed i
2 CONC n the 1866/1867 tax records where an agent for the wife of Hansford Alford is listed in tax records. A memorial government marker was placed in his memory at Swift Creek Cemetery near the graves of his daughters Mary Adeline Alfor
2 CONC d Roberts and Martha Ann Alford Dobson. Hansford Alford and his wives have numerous descendants in Florida.
