1 NAME Scrimzeour Cornwell /Furman/
2 GIVN Scrimzeour Cornwell
2 _MARNM Furman
1 NAME Major Scrimzeour C. Furman (CSA)
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 2 FEB 1835
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 AUG 1873
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/14564292/scrimzeour-cornwell-furman
2 CONT
2 CONT Major 2nd LA Cavalry C.S.A. Proud Confederate Soldier
2 CONT
2 CONT Furman, S. C., Capt. Pvt. Co. E, 2nd La. Cav. En. June 27, 1862, Pleasant Hill. Roll for Jan. and Feb., 1863. Present on detached service. Present on Roll for April 30, to Aug. 31, 1863. Captured near Natchitoches La., March 21, 1
2 CONC 864. Recd. at New Orleans, La., March 26, 1864.Appears on Roll of Prisoners of War, at New Orleans, La. Roll dated Office of Commsy. of Prisoners Dept., of the Gulf New Orleans, La., July 7, 1864. Transfd. from New Orleans, La., t
2 CONC o Mouth of Red River for Exchange Oct. 22, 1864.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Scrimzeour C. Furman was a medical doctor and a lieutenant in the "Pelican Rifles," which was the first unit from DeSoto Parish, Louisiana, to enter the Civil War. This unit which became Company D of the Second Louisiana Infantry 
2 CONC Regiment of the Army of Northern Virginia. Dr. Furman later funded and led Company E of the Second Louisiana Cavalry, which was popularly known as "Furman's Rangers".
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1858, Dr. Scrimzeour Cronwall Furman married Henry and Maria Marshall's daughter Mary T. Marshall; together, they had a daughter, Mary T. Furman (d. 1913). After the death of his wife Mary, S. C. Furman married her younger sist
2 CONC er, Mattie Marshall. This marriage produced a daughter, Maria Marshall Furman (nicknamed "Lulu).
