2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Raymond Fitts, 68, of Naval Base died at the Baptist Hospital at 8:15 a.m. today after three years of declining health. He was a native of Brunson, son of the late John Edwin Fitts and Mrs. Jeanette Amanda Reid Fitts. He wa
2 CONC s a member of the Charleston Heights Baptist Church and was an electrician at Savannah River Atomic Energy project. Surviving are his widow, Mrs. Beulah Harley Fitts of Naval Base; four daughters, Mrs. Harry Morrison of West Colum
2 CONC bia, Mrs. L. L. Young of Charleston, Mrs. William McManus and Mrs. Herbert Kull of Columbia; five sons, J. E. Fitts of Columbia, Walton R. Fitts of Augusta, Ga., Ralph R. Fitts of North Charleston, George H. Fitts of Naval Base an
2 CONC d Lt. Glenn L. Fitts of Parks Air Force Base, Calif.; 23 grandchildren; two great-grandchildren; two sisters, Mrs. Bessie Bradley of Bamberg and Mrs. W. H. Johnston of Kline; and a number of nieces and nephews. Funeral arrangement
2 CONC s are incomplete. The body will be at the Talbert Funeral Home until the services.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Record, Columbia, SC, 17 Oct 1952
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Robert Raymond Fitts, 68, of Naval Base, were to be conducted today at 4 p.m. at the Colonial Heights Baptist Church and burial was to be made in the Crescent Hill Memorial Park. Active pallbearers will meet a
2 CONC t the residence at 4:30 p.m. Sunday. Honorary pallbearers will meet at the church at 5 p.m. © The State, Columbia, SC, 18 Oct 1952
