2 CONT
2 CONT Walton Reid Fitts Sr., 65, of 109 Hillview Drive, Lexington, died Wednesday. Born in Parris Island, he was a son of the late Robert Raymond and Beulah Harley Fitts. Formerly of Charleston, he was a local resident for 39 years. He 
2 CONC was a World War II Army veteran, an electrician, and a member of American Legion Post No. 79, Moose Lodge, IBEW No. 382, and Platt Springs Unted Methodist Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife, Barbara Kinard Fitts; a daughter, Toni Zobel of Columbia; a son, Walton Fitts Jr. of Lexington; sisters, Raye Kull and Lydia McManus, both of Columbia, and Jeanette Young of New Buffalo, Mich.; and brothers
2 CONC , John Fitts of Gaston, George Fitts of West Columbia and Ralph Fitts of Charleston. Services will be held at 3 p.m. Friday at Platt Springs United Methodist Church, with burial in Southland Memorial Gardens. 
